.TH TULPAR-DOWNLOAD 1 "2026" "tulpar 0.1.0" "Tulpar Manual"
.SH NAME
tulpar-download \- fetch a package without installing it
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tulpar download
.RI [ options "] " name
.br
.B tulpar w
.RI [ options "] " name
.br
.B tulpar \-w
.RI [ options "] " name
.SH DESCRIPTION
Downloads the
.B .apg
archive and detached signature for
.I name
from the configured repositories, without installing it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIpath\fR
Write the downloaded archive to
.I path
instead of the default cache location under
.IR /var/cache/apg/pkgs/ .
.TP
.BI \-\-version " version"
Request a specific version instead of the first matching build.
.TP
.BI \-\-arch " arch"
Request a specific architecture.
.TP
.BI \-\-channel " channel"
Request a specific release channel. Defaults to
.IR stable .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, non-zero if the package could not be found or
downloaded.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tulpar (1),
.BR tulpar-install (1)
